  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM Activities in Iraq Outlined in the 2022 Syria Regional Refugee and Resilience Plan (3RP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to the needs of Syrian refugees and host communities as identified by the United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR) led Regional Refugee and Resilience Plan (3RP), of which IOM is a part, IOM will assist the Syrian refugees in Iraq, mainly by providing transportation from the border points to the refugee camps identified by the authorities of the Kurdistan Region of Iraq. Additionally, IOM will pursue its monitoring of the flows of population crossing the border through its Displacement Tracking Matrix, to provide the humanitarian actors with timely, accurate and up-to-date information on population movements at the border.</narrative>
  </description>
